<title>RUSSIA: Russian Duma adopts hard currency purchase tax.</title>
<headline>Russian Duma adopts hard currency purchase tax.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Russian Duma, the lower house of parliament, passed a draft law on a 0.5 percent tax on hard currency purchases by households, Interfax news agency said on Friday.</p>
<p>The Duma sent the draft to the Federation Council upper house for consideration, it said.</p>
<p>Last December the Duma passed the law, but it was turned down by Federation Council.</p>
<p>The government, which proposed the tax at 1.5 percent, had expected to get 2.3 trillion roubles from the tax in the first quarter.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
